WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
It was more like survival for us, so that if you ever,

2
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:08.820
ever had a point in your life that you could not survive, he [our father] taught us how to actually survive.

3
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:13.040
You could plant a garden, and get all the vegetables that you need.

4
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.200
And if you got chickens and ducks you can eat off of that.

5
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.540
And then he taught us how to fish.

6
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.740
If we had no means to get food, we knew how to get food.

7
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:29.520
It wasn't expensive to make a garden, and it wasn't that expensive to raise chickens, ducks, or whatever.

8
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.840
And fishing wasn't expensive, you just go in and catch fish, and fish were very plentiful back then.

9
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.320
We grew up with family that really wanted us to be able to know,

10
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:44.060
that whenever you get older and you have your own family, that your going to know what it's going to take to make it.

11
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:52.000
Even if you don't have money you still can make it, and that's what Mossville was all about, that's what our ancestors did.

12
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.760
They farmed, and they sold their crops and stuff like that.

13
00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.800
So our parents got it from them, and they brought it to us.

14
00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:03.500
And now we bring it on to our kids -- those that really want to get into it.
